      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SENZORA (2) has been very good at both of his outings. He rode the speed twice at this track when a very short-priced favourite and just found Open 3yo grade that bit hard second time of asking. He has a few gear changes here so if all is well, he has to be tough to beat. BARBARIAN KING (7) could pose a threat though. He was right around the mark in decent company each time and then trialled nicely since that resuming run. He may have that little bit more fitness. MARELLITY (8) has basically been around the same position in all her recent efforts. Probably finishes about the same here too. GYPSY'S DAUGHTER (6) was a winner first up so that could be important here. Might want some rain. BLUE TOES (3) will show speed but the gate could be tricky.",
